The MAX77836 LDOs support two operating modes via the PWRMD field in
CNFG1_LDO registers: normal and low-power (5 mA max load, reduced
quiescent current).  Implement the get_mode and set_mode callbacks
so consumers can switch between them.

The PWRMD field is the same register used for enable/disable and
controls the immediate operating mode, rather than a suspend-specific
behavior.  Use set_mode instead of the originally-requested
set_suspend_mode.

Remove the TODO comment that has been sitting here since the driver
was first added.

Signed-off-by: Jad Keskes <inasj268@gmail.com>
---
